// # types/ — Runtime Type Vocabulary
//
// Logline: The Oo* C structs (OoStr, OoResS, OoArena, OoThreadSlot, OoGpuDevice, ...). The split mirrors the .h file domains; each sub-header is the canonical home for one type family. The umbrella (types.h) pulls them all in via #include.
//
//
// Setup: Domain module. Caps and layout are in the parent ANCHOR.oo.
// Beats:
//   1. types.h — umbrella: #includes all 5 sub-headers.
//   2. types_str.h — OoStr, OoStrBuf, the string-literal macros.
//   3. types_num.h — OoI64, OoU64, OoSize, the int-width typedefs.
//   4. types_res.h — OoResS, the string-or-error result type.
//   5. types_actor.h — OoClosure, OoFlatEnvHeader, OoChannel (the actor-primitive types).
//   6. types_control.h — OoControlBlock, OoWeakRef, OO_FLAG_* (re-exported from core/mem/weak.h for canonical home).
//
// v2.3.0 file split: the original 384-line types.h was split into
// types.h (umbrella) + 6 sub-headers in types/. The split is purely
// organizational — the runtime ABI is unchanged; consumers that
// #include "types.h" still see the full surface.
//
// v3.1.0 audit cleanup: removed types/types_q.h (was a 8-line
// comment-only placeholder; the OoChannel type it was supposed to
// declare was actually defined in app/actor/actor_channel.c and is
// now typedef'd in types_actor.h). The umbrella is now 5 sub-headers
// instead of 6.
//
// ──▓▓ types ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: one type family per header — the canonical home ::
